        "original_id": "7b9a7c18-31bf-5db5-a770-857626cd5776",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pope Francis, Jorge Mario Bergoglio\n- Documents: Laudato si'\n- Organizations: Catholic Church\n- Places: Vatican City, Rome\n- Roles: Pope, Bishop of Rome, sovereign\n\nFacts:\n- Pope Francis was born as Jorge Mario Bergoglio on 17 December 1936.\n- Pope Francis is also rendered as Franciscus in Latin, Francesco in Italian, and Francisco in Spanish.\n- Pope Francis is the 266th and current Pope of the Catholic Church.\n- Pope Francis holds the title of Bishop of Rome ex officio and is the sovereign of Vatican City.\n- Laudato si' means “Praise be to you” in Medieval Central Italian.\n- Laudato si' is the second encyclical of Pope Francis.\n- Laudato si' has the subtitle “On Care For Our Common Home.”",
